00:30:50,048 --> 00:30:52,448
後付けのじゃって何なのじゃ？
What do you mean, "afterthought noja"?

444
00:30:52,548 --> 00:30:56,548
何？画像を拡大したらわかる後付けのじゃって何の話なのじゃ？
What? "If you zoom in on the image, you can tell it's an afterthought"—what are you talking about?

445
00:30:56,648 --> 00:30:58,848
ちょっと見せてやるか 主らに
Maybe I should show you guys.

446
00:30:58,948 --> 00:31:00,648
主らに見せてやるか
Should I show it to you guys?

447
00:31:00,948 --> 00:31:03,248
この不自然な...
This unnatural...

448
00:31:06,048 --> 00:31:07,548
ちっちゃくするか
Maybe I'll make it smaller.

449
00:31:07,548 --> 00:31:10,548
ま ちっちゃくしたらバレへんやろと思って
Well, I figured if I made it small, nobody would notice.

450
00:31:10,648 --> 00:31:11,748
よいしょ
All right.

451
00:31:11,748 --> 00:31:13,248
のじゃー
Noja~

452
00:31:13,548 --> 00:31:15,048
のじゃー
Noja~

453
00:31:15,248 --> 00:31:16,348
よいしょ
There we go.

454
00:31:16,548 --> 00:31:21,348
えーっと んでちょっと父の文章分かりづらかったから「どういう意味？」って聞いたら
Um, and since Dad's text was hard to understand, when I asked "What do you mean?"

455
00:31:21,548 --> 00:31:24,948
なんか「特に意味はなく 切り抜きされててびっくりした」
he said, "Nothing in particular, I was just shocked it got clipped."

456
00:31:25,048 --> 00:31:27,948
そう なんか切り抜きを見ていた側だったのに
Yeah, even though he was just someone who watched clips,

457
00:31:28,148 --> 00:31:33,648
なんか自分の言った発言のところが切り抜きされてる多分動画を見たのかの？
he probably watched a video where his own comment got clipped?

458
00:31:33,848 --> 00:31:36,648
なんか切り抜きされててびっくりしたし
He was shocked that it got clipped,

459
00:31:36,748 --> 00:31:39,048
ねねちが反応することにもびっくり
and also shocked that Nenechi reacted to it.

460
00:31:39,148 --> 00:31:44,248
父が...父が「ねねち」って言ってんの ちょっ ちょっと ちょっと嫌 ちょっと嫌なのじゃ
Hearing Dad... hearing my dad say "Nenechi", it's a bit... kind of gross, I kind of hate it, noja.

461
00:31:44,348 --> 00:31:45,948
ちょっと...ちょっと嫌なのじゃ
It's kind of... kind of gross, noja.

462
00:31:46,048 --> 00:31:48,048
うん「ねねちが反応することにもびっくり」
Yeah. "Also shocked that Nenechi reacted."

463
00:31:48,148 --> 00:31:50,848
ねねち呼びしてますやん ねねち呼びしてますやん
You're calling her "Nenechi"! You're calling her "Nenechi"!

464
00:31:50,948 --> 00:31:52,048
うん
Yeah.

465
00:31:52,548 --> 00:31:56,948
「XなどSNSから置いていかれた人は 反応に驚いている」
"People left behind by social media like X are stunned by the reaction."

466
00:31:56,948 --> 00:31:59,948
父がね 父あのSNSやってないから
Referring to my dad. Since Dad doesn't use social media.

467
00:32:00,148 --> 00:32:04,248
あの 驚いたらしい 反応に驚いてるらしい
So apparently he was surprised. Surprised by the reactions.

468
00:32:04,348 --> 00:32:05,148
うん
Yeah.

469
00:32:05,248 --> 00:32:06,848
びっくりしてたらしい
Apparently he was stunned.

470
00:32:06,948 --> 00:32:08,548
よかったね
Good for him.

471
00:32:08,848 --> 00:32:11,048
よかったね
Good for him.

472
00:32:11,248 --> 00:32:12,348
そう
Yeah.

473
00:32:12,448 --> 00:32:13,048
で
And,

474
00:32:13,148 --> 00:32:15,948
あと何かもう一個きたな
another message came in.

475
00:32:16,248 --> 00:32:19,448
ああ あと...で 追加で配信前に
Ah, and then... additionally, right before the stream,

476
00:32:19,548 --> 00:32:25,448
なんか「SNSで特殊なことが起こると舞い上がっちゃって 良くも悪くもいろいろ反応したくなるんだなと感じた
he said, "I felt that when something unusual happens on SNS, people get carried away and want to react in all sorts of ways, good or bad.

477
00:32:25,548 --> 00:32:30,848
アカウント無いけど これはまさに自主的に沈黙を貫く姿勢なのかも」じゃって
I don't have an account, but this might truly be a stance of voluntarily maintaining silence," noja.

478
00:32:31,048 --> 00:32:36,548
多分 ねね先輩に あの が 私信ツイートをしてくれて
Probably because Nene-senpai tweeted directly about it herself,

479
00:32:36,648 --> 00:32:39,848
「いいな」って思ってたVTuberの子が
a VTuber he liked...

480
00:32:40,048 --> 00:32:46,048
あのー 私信...から私信が飛んできて 嬉しかったんじゃろうね
well, a personal tweet came flying in from her, so he must have been so happy.

481
00:32:46,048 --> 00:32:48,548
めっちゃ嬉しかったっぽくて
He seemed super happy,

482
00:32:48,548 --> 00:32:51,348
あのー きっとそわそわしちゃったんじゃろうね
and he probably got all restless.

483
00:32:51,448 --> 00:32:55,748
「良くも悪くもいろいろ反応したくなるんだなと感じている」
"'I feel like people want to react in all kinds of ways, good or bad.'"

484
00:32:55,848 --> 00:32:56,848
うん
Yeah.

485
00:32:56,948 --> 00:32:59,848
「沈黙を貫く姿勢なのかも」だって
"'Maybe it's a stance of maintaining silence,' he says.

486
00:32:59,948 --> 00:33:02,448
で なんか一人で反省してた
And so he was reflecting all by himself.

487
00:33:02,448 --> 00:33:04,548
一人で反省してましたのじゃ
He was self-reflecting all on his own, noja.

488
00:33:04,548 --> 00:33:05,548
うん
Yeah.

489
00:33:06,548 --> 00:33:10,548
ってことがあったよっていうのを話そうと思って
So I wanted to share that that happened.

490
00:33:10,748 --> 00:33:14,948
あのー マシュマロで話したけどさ わし本当に記憶力がなくてさ
Um, I mentioned this on Marshmallow, but I really have a terrible memory,

491
00:33:15,048 --> 00:33:19,848
あのー 数日でさ 起こったこと忘れちゃうの
so within a few days, I completely forget what happened.

492
00:33:20,048 --> 00:33:24,048
新鮮な雑談ってさ 3日後には忘れてんの わし大体
Fresh chat topics, I usually forget them within three days.

493
00:33:24,248 --> 00:33:28,948
から早めに話そうと思って 早めに話したのじゃ
That's why I wanted to talk about it quickly, so I did, noja.

494
00:33:29,248 --> 00:33:31,948
「父も防災意識高い」
"'Your dad has high disaster prevention awareness too.'"

495
00:33:32,048 --> 00:33:34,948
まあ わしの父と母ね
Well, my mom and dad,

496
00:33:35,048 --> 00:33:38,948
え なんか主らの親世代って
hey, what about your parents' generation?

497
00:33:39,048 --> 00:33:40,948
どうじゃろう？
How are they, I wonder?

498
00:33:41,048 --> 00:33:44,248
インターネットリテラシーある？ない？
Do they have internet literacy? Or not?

499
00:33:44,548 --> 00:33:47,448
なんか結構人によるかなって思うんじゃけど
I guess it really depends on the person, but...

500
00:33:47,548 --> 00:33:51,948
父はね 父と母はね 結構インターネットリテラシー高いと思う
My dad, my dad and mom, I think their internet literacy is pretty high.

501
00:33:52,248 --> 00:33:54,848
うん SNSやってないし
Yeah. And they don't use social media.

502
00:33:55,048 --> 00:33:58,948
これが一番高い ガチ SNSやってないが一番高い気がする
Seriously, that makes it the highest. Not using SNS feels like the highest literacy.

503
00:33:59,248 --> 00:34:02,548
SNSやってないし あのー
They don't use SNS, and, well...

504
00:34:02,748 --> 00:34:06,948
両親ともにその友達がいないから 話す相手がいない
neither of my parents have friends, so they have no one to talk to.

505
00:34:07,148 --> 00:34:08,948
うん って言ってた
Yeah, that's what he said.

506
00:34:09,148 --> 00:34:13,548
そう「話す人がいないから大丈夫」って言ってた
Yeah, he said, "I don't have anyone to talk to, so I'm fine."

507
00:34:13,748 --> 00:34:15,548
うん のじゃ
Yeah, noja.

508
00:34:15,848 --> 00:34:17,348
うん
Yeah.

509
00:34:18,248 --> 00:34:23,848
あ ちなみに あの さっきね あの父とやり取りしてたメッセージアプリ
Oh, by the way, that messaging app I was using with Dad earlier,

510
00:34:23,948 --> 00:34:27,248
これ iMessageなんじゃけど
this is iMessage,

511
00:34:27,348 --> 00:34:30,448
なんでLINEとかじゃなくてiMessageでやり取りしてるかって言うと
but if you wonder why we use iMessage instead of LINE or something,

512
00:34:30,548 --> 00:34:34,548
あの 父友達いなさすぎてLINE持ってないんよね
it's because Dad has so few friends that he doesn't even have LINE.

513
00:34:34,648 --> 00:34:35,448
うん
Yeah.

514
00:34:35,548 --> 00:34:39,948
なんか交換する人がいない 特にないから
Like, there's no one to exchange contacts with, so...

515
00:34:40,048 --> 00:34:44,848
一生...一生備え付けの 一生備え付けのやつで
forever... he just uses the pre-installed, pre-installed one

516
00:34:45,048 --> 00:34:48,448
メッセージしてるんじゃよね
to send messages.

517
00:34:48,548 --> 00:34:49,448
うん
Yeah.

518
00:34:49,548 --> 00:34:50,548
そう
Yeah.

519
00:34:51,248 --> 00:34:52,948
実は
In fact.

520
00:34:56,648 --> 00:34:58,948
「リテラシー高いと言える」確かに！
"'You could say his literacy is high.' Indeed!

521
00:34:59,048 --> 00:35:00,048
確かに！
Indeed!

522
00:35:00,756 --> 00:35:01,356
のじゃ
Indeed.

523
00:35:01,456 --> 00:35:02,156
うん
Yeah.

524
00:35:02,956 --> 00:35:03,656
うん
Mm-hm.

525
00:35:05,056 --> 00:35:05,856
そう
Right.

526
00:35:06,156 --> 00:35:09,556
だから一応メッセージでね やり取りしてるのじゃ
So for now, we've been keeping in touch via messages.

527
00:35:09,656 --> 00:35:10,556
のじゃ
Yep.

528
00:35:14,256 --> 00:35:15,056
よし
Alright.

529
00:35:15,256 --> 00:35:17,356
30分ぐらい いい時間なんじゃない？
Around 30 minutes, isn't that a good length?

530
00:35:17,356 --> 00:35:19,456
アーカイブめっちゃ見やすいんじゃない？
The archive should be super easy to watch, right?

531
00:35:19,456 --> 00:35:21,556
話したいこと全部話したのじゃん
And I covered everything I wanted to talk about!

532
00:35:21,756 --> 00:35:23,556
話したいこと全部話した
I said everything I wanted to say.

533
00:35:24,656 --> 00:35:25,856
いいんじゃない？
Isn't that great?

534
00:35:29,156 --> 00:35:30,456
